  "tail_text": "edit_distance` by implementing the classic Levenshtein DP algorithm.\n\nunicaa01_p25_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Levenshtein edit distance.\"\"\"\ndef edit_distance(a, b):\n    m, n = len(a), len(b)\n    # Initialize DP table with (n+1) columns and (m+1) rows\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        dp[0][j] = j\n    # Fill table\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1\n            dp[i][j] = min(\n                dp[i - 1][j] + 1,        # deletion\n                dp[i][j - 1] + 1,        # insertion\n                dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost  # substitution\n            )\n    return dp[m][n]\n\ndef demo():\n    return edit_distance(\"kitten\", \"sitting\")\n```",
  "full_completion_text": "edit_distance` by implementing the classic Levenshtein DP algorithm.\n\nunicaa01_p25_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Levenshtein edit distance.\"\"\"\ndef edit_distance(a, b):\n    m, n = len(a), len(b)\n    # Initialize DP table with (n+1) columns and (m+1) rows\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(m + 1)]\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = i\n    for j in range(n + 1):\n        dp[0][j] = j\n    # Fill table\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        for j in range(1, n + 1):\n            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1\n            dp[i][j] = min(\n                dp[i - 1][j] + 1,        # deletion\n                dp[i][j - 1] + 1,        # insertion\n                dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost  # substitution\n            )\n    return dp[m][n]\n\ndef demo():\n    return edit_distance(\"kitten\", \"sitting\")\n```",
